From f6da14ace940e5a11b18c13434a6d883d93b6ca7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:40:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/88] h713: one reader for the IR decoder while asleep

Asleep, every pass stepped the same decoder twice: system.c's cir_poll(),
which knows only CONFIG_CIR_WAKE_CODE (0x00ff14) and writes no wake word,
and h713_wake_poll(), which matches the 19 cir_param codes and writes 0x9b.
A frame completed in the first call was lost for the second: codes of other
remotes woke about every other time, and the projector's own key often
woke with wake word 0. With the H713 code list the generic reader is not
taken; h713_wake_poll() is the only one (0x00ff14 is the list's first entry).

Review finding B26 (07.10.2026), confirmed in the code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 common/system.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common/system.c b/common/system.c
index 823236a..69b782c 100644
--- a/common/system.c
+++ b/common/system.c
@@ -182,7 +182,10 @@ system_state_machine(uint32_t exception)
 			 * the R_PIO state the CIR pin setup would change. */
 			h713_suspend_prepare();
 			cec = cec_get();
-			cir = cir_get();
+			/* With the H713's code list, h713_wake_poll() reads the
+			 * decoder itself; a second reader here would take every
+			 * other frame away from it. */
+			cir = CONFIG(H713_IR_WAKE_NECX) ? NULL : cir_get();
 
 			/* Configure the SoC for minimal power consumption. */
 			record_step(STEP_SUSPEND_DRAM);
